    {
      "id": "claim_67a5ddeba80547c8b2a098e089e01adb",
      "statement": "title_hit uses regex r'\\b{token}(?:js|s|\\d+)?\\b' matching whole words with optional plural/version/js suffix; there is no <4 char special case. Suffixes are allowed (python3, reactjs, agents) but prefixes are not (rust does not match anti-trust, java does not match javascript).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent.py#L191-L199",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9be826f93953bd3893d7519b825061d4d7e8dbb27510cafdb059e53168bc7fd1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_24f697c1fa184b7f8f238b9ee14891cd",
      "statement": "score_job is frequency-weighted: title_hits*TITLE_WEIGHT plus a description contribution of min(desc_hits + gen_hits + freq/8, 9), where gen_hits counts GENERIC words in the title (0 when the whole query is generic) and freq/8 is a frequency bonus. The description contribution is capped at 9, below TITLE_WEIGHT=10, so it can only reorder admitted results, never admit a job the title did not match.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent.py#L202-L221",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:83f64c2ce9b0502f419876755a59d17544b82edde03daa3d1af3d526f78a35ba:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cea7bf93376b4f4ca4b6ddf6cf0dd397",
      "statement": "collect_results deduplicates by a company+title hash (re.sub removing non-alphanumeric), not by apply_url, and keeps only jobs passing location_ok(job, country) and job_is_recent(job) (MAX_AGE_DAYS=120); it then keeps score >= TITLE_WEIGHT, sorts by score descending, and caps at MAX_RESULTS=12.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent.py#L521-L544",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f90cc87eaf1337f3cd44dffdbd79102388251a153f3eaf7b06c808e6184bf47a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_370c8c720e44439ca5b8c377533dc377",
      "statement": "fetch_wjobs (Workable) is a two-round crawl: workable_urls fetches search pages and extracts links from schema.org ItemList LD+JSON using path-form URLs (/search/<country>/remote-<token>-jobs) because robots.txt disallows the query-string form; the country segment is mandatory ('worldwide' slug) and an unknown country returns 200 with an empty list, retried worldwide. workable_job then fetches each surviving posting's JobPosting LD+JSON block, capped at WORKABLE_DETAILS=6 per-posting fetches.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent.py#L355-L453",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6e1e29581984f404f8bec9478b9dbc564009edbea83e06d30c18386d56da1f79:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7ddc1b6138b14078bb2c33a07b3e5f2e",
      "statement": "fetch_jobs (RemoteOK) uses distinctive_tokens (not just the first keyword), tries tags in order until a page returns >= ENOUGH (50) results, deduplicates by URL/id across tag attempts, and re-checks every listing against its own title via title_hit because RemoteOK tags are SEO filler.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent.py#L279-L307",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b61c8bc78c889ebc91db4418521ba03d8538ce80c9c835488b6d36e9a6b2033a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_247847cab8f548a580edd95698836540",
      "statement": "fetch_tjobs (Remotive) is a cached feed, not a search: remotive_feed() uses a module-level _REMOTIVE dict with REMOTIVE_TTL=6*3600 (6h); the edge cache does not vary on query string, a failed refresh keeps the previous list, and listings are filtered by title_hit in the fetcher.",
      "evidence": [
        {
